  "challenge": "The packet already resolves this without a human: WidgetA’s contracted reference is $250 (get_item_reference), PR-001’s rule is a hard overcharge test (unit price > reference × 1.05), and the rush line at $300 fails it by 20% with no rush schedule, PO authorization, or prior accepted rush premium anywhere in vendor history (Consolidated Materials Group has zero prior invoices). PR-003’s own policy only flags dual pricing for the Adjudicator to decide—it does not create an exception to PR-001—and a free-text “(rush order)” label is not a contracted rate. Other lines match reference exactly, so the sole defect is an uncontracted premium that should be rejected and sent back for rebill at $250 (or $250 plus a separate, authorized rush fee), not parked in escalation.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["PR-001", "PR-003"]
}
